@testray.main.component.name = "Support QA"
@type = "osb.integration"

Feature: Koroneiki Product To OSB Integration
	Testing Koroneiki Product Integration to osb functionality.

Setup:
	* I get all test passwords and admin emails

Teardown:
	* I tear down the products on koroneiki with the following names
	| A Liferay OSB Product        |
	| A Liferay Server Product     |
	| A New Liferay OSB Product    |
	| A New Liferay Server Product |

Scenario: Create and view product
	@ help.center.acceptance = "true"
	@ help.center.smoke = "true"
	Koroneiki products created via API should be viewable on OSB.

	Given I create a product with the following values
	| Name | A Liferay OSB Product | |
	And I log into the support homepage as "${staticSupportAdminEmailAdress}" with password "${staticSupportAdminPassword}"
	And I go to the OSB admin main page
	Then I should be able to view a product with the name "A Liferay OSB Product" and the following values
	| Name                  | A Liferay OSB Product |
	| Koroneiki Product Key | Verify from name      |

Scenario: Create and view multiple products
	Multiple products created via API should be viewable on OSB.

	Given I create a product with the following values
	| Name | A Liferay OSB Product | |
	And I create a product with the following values
	| Name | A Liferay Server Product | |
	And I log into the support homepage as "${staticSupportAdminEmailAdress}" with password "${staticSupportAdminPassword}"
	And I go to the OSB admin main page
	Then I should be able to view a product with the name "A Liferay OSB Product" and the following values
	| Name                  | A Liferay OSB Product |
	| Koroneiki Product Key | Verify from name      |
	And I should be able to view a product with the name "A Liferay Server Product" and the following values
	| Name                  | A Liferay Server Product |
	| Koroneiki Product Key | Verify from name         |

Scenario: Update and view product
	Koroneiki products updated via API should be viewable on OSB.

	Given I create a product with the following values
	| Name | A Liferay OSB Product | |
	And I update a product with the name "A Liferay OSB Product" to have the following values
	| Name | A Liferay Server Product | |
	And I log into the support homepage as "${staticSupportAdminEmailAdress}" with password "${staticSupportAdminPassword}"
	And I go to the OSB admin main page
	Then I should be able to view a product with the name "A Liferay Server Product" and the following values
	| Name                  | A Liferay Server Product |
	| Koroneiki Product Key | Verify from name         |
	And I should not be able to view a product with the name "A Liferay OSB Product"

Scenario: Update and view multiple products
	Multiple products updated via API should be viewable on OSB.

	Given I create a product with the following values
	| Name | A Liferay OSB Product | |
	And I create a product with the following values
	| Name | A Liferay Server Product | |
	And I update a product with the name "A Liferay OSB Product" to have the following values
	| Name | A New Liferay OSB Product | |
	And I update a product with the name "A Liferay Server Product" to have the following values
	| Name | A New Liferay Server Product | |
	And I log into the support homepage as "${staticSupportAdminEmailAdress}" with password "${staticSupportAdminPassword}"
	And I go to the OSB admin main page
	Then I should be able to view a product with the name "A New Liferay OSB Product" and the following values
	| Name                  | A New Liferay OSB Product |
	| Koroneiki Product Key | Verify from name          |
	And I should be able to view a product with the name "A New Liferay Server Product" and the following values
	| Name                  | A New Liferay Server Product |
	| Koroneiki Product Key | Verify from name             |
	And I should not be able to view a product with the name "A Liferay OSB Product"
	And I should not be able to view a product with the name "A Liferay Server Product"

Scenario: Remove product and view
	Koroneiki products removed via API should not be viewable on OSB.

	Given I create a product with the following values
	| Name | A Liferay OSB Product | |
	And I delete a koroneiki product with the name "A Liferay OSB Product"
	And I log into the support homepage as "${staticSupportAdminEmailAdress}" with password "${staticSupportAdminPassword}"
	And I go to the OSB admin main page
	Then I should not be able to view a product with the name "A Liferay OSB Product"

Scenario: Remove multiple products and view
	Multiple products removed via API should not be viewable on OSB.

	Given I create a product with the following values
	| Name | A Liferay OSB Product | |
	And I create a product with the following values
	| Name | A Liferay Server Product | |
	And I delete a koroneiki product with the name "A Liferay OSB Product"
	And I delete a koroneiki product with the name "A Liferay Server Product"
	And I log into the support homepage as "${staticSupportAdminEmailAdress}" with password "${staticSupportAdminPassword}"
	And I go to the OSB admin main page
	Then I should not be able to view a product with the name "A Liferay OSB Product"
	And I should not be able to view a product with the name "A Liferay Server Product"

Scenario: Create and view product external link
	Koroneiki product external links created via API should be viewable on OSB.

	Given I create a product with the following values
	| Name | A Liferay OSB Product | |
	And I create an external link on a product "A Liferay OSB Product" with the following values
	| Domain      | liferayosb |
	| Entity Id   | 1234       |
	| Entity Name | LiferayOSB |
	And I create a nested field for the product external link with the following values
	| Domain      | liferayosb |
	| Entity Id   | 1234       |
	| Entity Name | LiferayOSB |
	And I log into the support homepage as "${staticSupportAdminEmailAdress}" with password "${staticSupportAdminPassword}"
	And I go to the OSB admin main page
	Then I should be able to view a product with the name "A Liferay OSB Product" and the following values
	| Name                      | A Liferay OSB Product |
	| Koroneiki Product Key     | Verify from name      |
	| External Link Domain      | liferayosb            |
	| External Link Entity Id   | 1234                  |
	| External Link Entity Name | LiferayOSB            |

Scenario: Remove product external link and view
	Koroneiki product external links removed via API should not be viewable on OSB.

	Given I create a product with the following values
	| Name | A Liferay OSB Product | |
	And I create an external link on a product "A Liferay OSB Product" with the following values
	| Domain      | liferayosb |
	| Entity Id   | 1234       |
	| Entity Name | LiferayOSB |
	And I delete an external link with the entity id "1234" on the product "A Liferay OSB Product"
	And I log into the support homepage as "${staticSupportAdminEmailAdress}" with password "${staticSupportAdminPassword}"
	And I go to the OSB admin main page
	Then I should not be able to view a product "A Liferay OSB Product" external link with the domain "liferayosb" and entity name "LiferayOSB" and entity id "1234"